# lane_host: step-ahead (TF_DS_STEP_AHEAD=1, rank 0; recipe setting STEP_AHEAD, off by default). When a reply ends and
# nothing else runs or waits, a background prompt pass reads the reply after its prompt (prompt ++ reply, cut at the last
# chunk end of the family's grid that leaves its tail) and keeps the state there while the client runs its tools. An
# agent's next request (prompt ++ reply ++ tool results) then resumes past its own previous reply instead of reading it
# again. Up to the kept point the pass is that request's own cold pass (the same grid, the same tokens), so replies keep
# their bits; a reply the client renders back differently resumes where it did before.
# - A queued pass yields to any arrival, a running one is cancelled by an arrival it is not the prefix of, and a pass never
#   runs beside another stream. "Nothing else runs or waits" counts the queue and the ready, loading and deferred lists
#   (waitingCount()), and a pass with anything queued behind it is dropped.
# - A pass never parks on a disk restore: it resumes from what memory holds, or computes from its start.
# - deliver(): a finished job leaves `admitted` before finish() frees it, so a submission that walks `admitted` under the
#   lock never meets a freed job (a use-after-free with the switch off too). Every caller is changed, fbbc971's fillOne
#   included. The yielded list's room is reserved before a queued pass leaves the queue; the kept count and log line fire
#   only when keepWith kept the state at the pass's point (else an unkept count and line).
# - With fbbc971's prompt pass in pieces: step-ahead stays off while TF_FILL_CHUNKS is set (as 0005's interleave rule
#   does), a pass waits while another pass fills, and a pass that meets ContextFull is dropped, not requeued.
# Host tests (lane_host.zig, lane_host_reuse_test.zig): a finished job is out of `admitted` at .finished, step-ahead off
# and on; a queued pass goes when a request waits behind it; a reply's own tokens are read and the next step resumes past
# them with the same tokens; nothing runs when off, and a refused keep counts as not kept.
# History: #41 (Coinupbtc, on 629c524), rebased by Braincramps in #66; the #66 review fixes by Hector Isaza (hecisaza);
# rebased onto fbbc971 and 0001-0038 here. Measurements: in the pull request.
